  "reasoning": "The defendant Wang and his wife destroyed a police inquiry record and then violently resisted police officers attempting to detain him. During the resistance, a police officer sustained a light injury (abrasions and a rib fracture). This conduct constitutes obstruction of public duties (妨害公务罪) under Article 277 of the Criminal Law, which covers assaulting or resisting police officers performing official duties and causing injury. No other criminal elements such as illegal possession of weapons, forgery of state documents, or theft are present. Therefore, the appropriate charge is 妨害公务.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]妨害公务<eoa>"
}

